  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "about",
      "tabLabel": "About",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Jamaican Dominoes",
          "subtitle": "Caribbean Draw Game",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Jamaican dominoes: Caribbean draw game. Four players; partner or cut-throat (no partner). Double-six."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Domino games are enthusiastically played across the Caribbean; in Jamaica the style is boisterous and pieces are often slammed on the table. Two main forms are played: Partner (fixed partnerships, favoured in world tournaments) and Cut Throat (each player for himself), with contributions documented from JamDom.com and local players."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Four players for Partner or Cut Throat; partners sit opposite at a square table."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Double-six domino set of 28 tiles (0-0 through 6-6), known as bones."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Tiles"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Each player receives 7 bones; in Cut Throat with 4 players each gets 7; remaining tiles form the boneyard."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Variations",
          "subtitle": "Known ways this game changes",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "style": "unordered",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Partner: Four players in fixed partnerships; first to 6 points (opponents 0) wins."
                },
                {
                  "text": "Cut Throat: Each player for himself; first to 6 wins provided another has 0."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
